263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 132 0 R
/T (Ethics)
/E (Ethics)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 502 0 R
/E (This study investigates the relationship between sustained academic activity and cognitive engagement, quantified using EEG-derived engagement indices during a 30-minute work session. Conclusions are limited to short-term observations within a controlled experimental setting, and no claims are made regarding long-term cognitive effects.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 503 0 R
/E (The study qualifies under Low Risk Human Participation guidelines as per Youth Science Canada. The EEG device used \(Muse headband\) is non-invasive and comparable to commercially available wearable technology. Experimental tasks are similar in nature to typical academic activities. Potential risks are minimal and may include temporary mental fatigue or mild physical discomfort from wearing the headband. Participants were informed that they could withdraw at any time without penalty.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 504 0 R
/E (Participation was fully voluntary. The study does not promote or advocate for mandatory cognitive monitoring in educational settings. Any potential future applications of attentional monitoring technologies should prioritize individual autonomy, informed consent, and ethical oversight.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 505 0 R
/E (EEG recordings are treated as sensitive biometric data. Each participant was assigned a coded identifier, and no personally identifying information was attached to the dataset. All data were stored locally on a password-protected device accessible only to the researcher. Only aggregated, anonymized results are reported.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 506 0 R
/E (This research does not diagnose cognitive fatigue, attention disorders, or neurological conditions. Findings are exploratory and correlational in nature, and interpretations are presented conservatively to avoid overstating the capabilities of consumer-grade EEG technology.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
